<div class="narrow">
<h1>Accessibility and help</h1>
<p class="lead">VisionConnect Jobs is built for people with all kinds of disabilities. This page explains what is built in and how to get the most from it.</p>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-sr">
    <h2 id="h-sr">Using a screen reader</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Every page has one main heading. Press <kbd>H</kbd> (NVDA / JAWS) or use the rotor (VoiceOver) to move between headings.</li>
        <li>The first links on every page are <strong>Skip to main content</strong> and <strong>Skip to navigation</strong>.</li>
        <li>Form errors are read out automatically. A list of problems appears at the top, and each item takes you to the field.</li>
        <li>On job pages, the link <strong>Jump to apply</strong> takes you straight to the apply section.</li>
        <li>Buttons that switch on and off, like <strong>Save job</strong>, announce their state, for example “pressed”.</li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-low">
    <h2 id="h-low">If you have low vision</h2>
    <p>Open <strong>Accessibility settings</strong> at the top of any page to change the text size (three levels), switch to Dark or High contrast colours, widen the spacing, or turn animations off. Your choices are saved on this device. You can also zoom the browser up to 400% and the page will reflow without sideways scrolling.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-deaf">
    <h2 id="h-deaf">If you are deaf or hard of hearing</h2>
    <p>The whole site is text based, with no audio needed. In your profile, choose how you want to be interviewed, for example text chat, a sign language interpreter or video with live captions. Employers see this before they contact you.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-mob">
    <h2 id="h-mob">If you have a mobility or motor disability</h2>
    <p>You can use the whole site with a keyboard, voice commands, a switch device or eye tracking. Buttons and links are large and spaced apart. Jobs show whether remote work, flexible hours, a wheelchair-accessible workspace or accessible transport is offered.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-cog">
    <h2 id="h-cog">If you find reading or forms hard</h2>
    <p>We use short sentences, one idea per step and clear error messages. Wide spacing and larger text in Accessibility settings can also make pages calmer to read. Quick apply sends your saved profile in one step.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-keys">
    <h2 id="h-keys">Using the keyboard</h2>
    <dl class="dl">
        <dt><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></dt><dd>Move to the next or previous link, button or field.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Enter</kbd></dt><dd>Open a link or press a button.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Space</kbd></dt><dd>Tick a box or press a button.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Arrow keys</kbd></dt><dd>Choose between radio buttons, or change a drop-down list.</dd>
        <dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt><dd>Close the Accessibility settings panel.</dd>
    </dl>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-voice">
    <h2 id="h-voice">Voice commands and reading aloud</h2>
    <p>In <strong>Accessibility settings</strong>, press <strong>Start voice commands</strong> and speak. This works in Google Chrome and Microsoft Edge. You can choose English, Hindi or Marathi. Examples:</p>
    <ul>
        <li>“Jobs”, “home”, “profile”, “applications”, “saved”, “dashboard”, “log in”, “help”</li>
        <li>“Search for accountant” opens job search with that keyword</li>
        <li>“Read page” reads the page aloud. “Stop” stops it</li>
        <li>“Bigger text”, “dark mode”, “high contrast”</li>
    </ul>
    <p>नोकरी, प्रोफाइल, होम, मदत जैसे शब्द हिंदी और मराठी में भी काम करते हैं / चालतात.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-priv">
    <h2 id="h-priv">Your privacy</h2>
    <p>Your disability details, UDID number and resume are visible only to you and to employers whose jobs you apply to. Resumes are stored privately and are never public links.</p>
</section>

<section class="section" aria-labelledby="h-prob">
    <h2 id="h-prob">Found a barrier?</h2>
    <p>If something on this site is hard to use with your tools, please tell the VisionConnect team. We treat accessibility problems as bugs and fix them first.</p>
</section>
</div>
